sequenceDiagram
%% Maps to EA diagram: UML Sequence (high-level overview)
%% Purpose: show end-to-end resolution cycle with bounded response,
%% asynchronous engine processing, and convergence via lookup.

%% External client
participant Originator as "Originator"

box "Entity Resolution System (ERSys)"
    participant ERIntake as "Entity Resolution Intake Service"
    participant CanonicalLookup as "Canonical Lookup Service"
    participant ERS as "Entity Resolution Service (ERS)"
end

participant MessagingMiddleware as "Messaging Middleware"

box "Entity Resolution Engine (ERE)"
    participant ERE as "Entity Resolution Engine (ERE)"
end

%% --- Client-facing bounded resolve ---
Originator ->> ERIntake: Resolve Entity Mention <br> (request identifiers + EntityMention)
ERIntake ->> ERS: Validate and register request (idempotent)
ERS ->> ERS: Derive deterministic canonical identifier &<br> ensure a Resolution Decision exists
ERS -->> ERIntake: Draft canonical identifier <br> + outcome status (bounded)
ERIntake -->> Originator: Draft canonical identifier <br>+ outcome status (bounded)

%% --- Asynchronous resolution ---
ERS ->> MessagingMiddleware: Publish resolution request <br> (request identifiers + EntityMention)
MessagingMiddleware ->> ERE: Deliver request (async)

ERE ->> MessagingMiddleware: Publish candidate alignments <br> (candidates & confidence scores)
MessagingMiddleware ->> ERS: Deliver results (async)

ERS ->> ERS: Integrate candidates under decision-centric governance
%%note right of ERS: ERS remains sole authority for canonical identity and decisions.

%% --- Convergence via lookup ---
Originator ->> CanonicalLookup: Lookup canonical assignment <br> (originatorId, originatorRequestId, entityType)
CanonicalLookup ->> ERS: Retrieve current governed assignment
ERS -->> CanonicalLookup: Current canonical identifier + statusus
CanonicalLookup -->> Originator: Current canonical identifier
